From 0c46a10d915538b68bbda4abcebc6c9ad390fb5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:10:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] freeholdos: report real quiesce failures and ignore a
 decoy registration whose user no longer exists

freeholdos: report real quiesce failures and re-evaluate the user-switcher state

Squash of former patches:

- 0085 test: add coverage for RealUserQuiescer's per-process freeze failure
- 0086 freeholdos: make RealUserQuiescer report real per-process freeze failure
- 0087 freeholdos: re-evaluate the user-switcher StateFlow on keyguard transitions
- 0088 systemui: migrate ReferenceGlobalRootComponent to Kotlin
- 0089 systemui: break UserRepositoryImpl's Dagger dependency cycle
- 0090 systemui: actually defer keyguardRepository.get() past construction
- 0091 freeholdos: fix RealUserQuiescerTest checked-exception compile error
- 0092 freeholdos: mock ProcessRecord under the shared dexmaker classloader
- 0093 freeholdos: fix UserRepositoryImplTest to pass a Lazy<KeyguardRepository>

freeholdos: ignore a decoy registration whose user no longer exists

The decoy registration is not cleared when the decoy user is removed. A wrong
PIN then verified against the removed user, which threw
IllegalArgumentException out of the rate limiter's stats write, crashed SystemUI
and briefly blanked the screen. Treat such a registration as no decoy, with the
same equivalent-cost dummy check.
